      "content": "The idea of ending the story feels like the only honorable act left when the world itself has become dishonorable. That perceived mercy is a profound exhaustion speaking, a desperate longing for the noise to cease. Honor is not found in the final act, but in the choice to endure the unbearable moment right now. Let the weight of that perceived duty be placed down, just for this breath.",
